window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b178-24c5148c260883e8.json"]={sha256:"24c5148c260883e883816a4ff21090b18242ce716d23603830d19c555a728ea2",value:{"id":"b178","title":"地下岩洞穹頂支護","titleEn":"Underground cavern crown support","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"大跨度岩洞的穩定同時受到節理幾何、開挖卸載、支護剛度及三維交叉口影響。本課分開討論可脫落楔塊與整體岩體拱效應，讓學徒用力學模型、應變監測及反算辨別真正的荷載路徑，再檢查地震與排水退化如何改變既有支護的需求。","summaryEn":"Large-span cavern stability depends on joints, excavation unloading, support stiffness and three-dimensional intersections. This course distinguishes detachable wedges from rock-mass arching, uses force models, strain monitoring and back-analysis to identify load paths, and evaluates how seismic action and drainage deterioration change support demand.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-trenchless","subcategoryTitle":"無開挖、豎井與岩洞","subcategoryTitleEn":"Trenchless works, shafts and caverns","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-trenchless","learningTags":["underground","ug-trenchless","cavern"],"architectureFamily":"cavern","architectureNodes":[["節理楔塊","Joint wedge"],["岩拱應力","Rock-arch stress"],["錨索分力","Cable support component"],["交叉口開口率","Intersection opening ratio"],["地震慣性","Seismic inertia"],["排水與接觸力","Drainage and contact force"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[3,0]],"diagram":{"type":"cavern","labels":["節理楔塊","岩拱應力","錨索分力","交叉口開口率","地震慣性"],"labelsEn":["Joint wedge","Rock-arch stress","Cable support component","Intersection opening ratio","Seismic inertia"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創教學例：假設穹頂可動楔塊體積V=12 m³，岩石單位重γ=26 kN/m³，重量W=γV=312 kN。若地質測繪使估計體積增加10%至13.2 m³，重量增為343.2 kN，增加31.2 kN。這個結果只修改重力項，不表示所需錨力也一定按相同比例增加，因為楔塊形狀改變可能同時影響節理接觸面、出露方向與錨索穿越位置。必須重新建立三維自由體圖，檢查水壓、摩擦及錨固，再用獨立地質觀測確認模型。","textEn":"Original teaching example: assume a potentially movable crown wedge of V=12 m³ and rock unit weight γ=26 kN/m³. Its weight is W=γV=312 kN. If mapping increases the estimated volume by 10% to 13.2 m³, weight becomes 343.2 kN, an increase of 31.2 kN. This changes gravity only; required cable force need not increase by the same percentage because revised geometry may also change joint contact area, daylighting direction and cable intersections. Rebuild the three-dimensional free body, check water pressure, friction and anchorage, and corroborate the geometry with independent geological observations.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b178-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「節理楔塊的機理與驗證」與「岩拱應力的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Joint wedge mechanism and verification\" and \"Rock-arch stress mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b178-v14-01","title":"節理楔塊的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint wedge mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「節理楔塊」如何影響地下岩洞穹頂支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Joint wedge” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Underground cavern crown support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"岩洞穹頂的節理組合可能界定一塊能向洞內移動的岩塊，即使完整岩石強度很高也不保證穩定。楔塊是否形成取決於節理傾向、傾角及延續性，不能只從單一剖面推斷；重量則是滑移或掉落分析的基本荷載。重量計算不包含節理剪力、地下水與支護反力，亦不等於所需錨力；先證明可動方向，再建立相應自由體圖。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「節理楔塊」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Intersecting joints may define a block capable of moving into the cavern even when intact rock is strong. Formation depends on joint dip, direction and persistence and cannot be inferred from one section alone. Block weight is the basic load for a sliding or falling mechanism. Weight alone excludes joint shear, water and support reactions and is not the required anchor force; establish admissible movement before drawing the corresponding free body. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Joint wedge” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：岩石單位重γ=26 kN/m³、假設楔塊體積V=12 m³，W=γV=312 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: With rock unit weight γ=26 kN/m³ and assumed wedge volume V=12 m³, W=γV=312 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「完整岩石抗壓強度很高就不會有穹頂落塊。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"High intact-rock compressive strength prevents cavern-crown block falls.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「節理楔塊」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Joint wedge”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-01-k1","title":"節理楔塊的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Joint wedge mechanism and verification","text":"岩洞穹頂的節理組合可能界定一塊能向洞內移動的岩塊，即使完整岩石強度很高也不保證穩定。楔塊是否形成取決於節理傾向、傾角及延續性，不能只從單一剖面推斷；重量則是滑移或掉落分析的基本荷載。","textEn":"Intersecting joints may define a block capable of moving into the cavern even when intact rock is strong. Formation depends on joint dip, direction and persistence and cannot be inferred from one section alone.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：完整岩石抗壓強度很高就不會有穹頂落塊。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: High intact-rock compressive strength prevents cavern-crown block falls. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「節理楔塊的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint wedge mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["完整岩石抗壓強度很高就不會有穹頂落塊。","岩洞穹頂的節理組合可能界定一塊能向洞內移動的岩塊，即使完整岩石強度很高也不保證穩定。","上覆岩重全部直接落在噴凝土薄殼上。"],"optionsEn":["High intact-rock compressive strength prevents cavern-crown block falls.","Intersecting joints may define a block capable of moving into the cavern even when intact rock is strong.","All overburden weight acts directly on the thin shotcrete shell."],"answer":1,"explanation":"岩洞穹頂的節理組合可能界定一塊能向洞內移動的岩塊，即使完整岩石強度很高也不保證穩定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Intersecting joints may define a block capable of moving into the cavern even when intact rock is strong. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b178-v14-02","title":"節理楔塊的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint wedge mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「節理楔塊」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Joint wedge” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：岩石單位重γ=26 kN/m³、假設楔塊體積V=12 m³，W=γV=312 kN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: With rock unit weight γ=26 kN/m³ and assumed wedge volume V=12 m³, W=γV=312 kN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用掌子面與穹頂測繪建立三維節理面，對可能出露的塊體核對延續性與體積，不把所有交線當真實裂面。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build three-dimensional joint planes from face and crown mapping, verifying persistence and volume of potentially daylighting blocks rather than treating every intersection as a real release surface.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：岩石單位重γ=26 kN/m³、假設楔塊體積V=12 m³，W=γV=312 kN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: With rock unit weight γ=26 kN/m³ and assumed wedge volume V=12 m³, W=γV=312 kN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「節理楔塊的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint wedge mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["錨索總張力直接相加就是任意方向的支護力。","量到應變後乘上固定模數即可得到精確永久應力。","原創教學假設：岩石單位重γ=26 kN/m³、假設楔塊體積V=12 m³，W=γV=312 kN。"],"optionsEn":["Adding cable tensions directly gives support resistance in every direction.","Measured strain times one constant modulus gives exact permanent stress.","Original teaching assumptions: With rock unit weight γ=26 kN/m³ and assumed wedge volume V=12 m³, W=γV=312 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：岩石單位重γ=26 kN/m³、假設楔塊體積V=12 m³，W=γV=312 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: With rock unit weight γ=26 kN/m³ and assumed wedge volume V=12 m³, W=γV=312 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b178-v14-03","title":"節理楔塊的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint wedge mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「節理楔塊」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Joint wedge” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用掌子面與穹頂測繪建立三維節理面，對可能出露的塊體核對延續性與體積，不把所有交線當真實裂面。地質模型應保留節理可信度及未曝光區；開挖暴露新節理後，由地工設計者重核楔塊支護需求。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build three-dimensional joint planes from face and crown mapping, verifying persistence and volume of potentially daylighting blocks rather than treating every intersection as a real release surface. Retain joint-confidence levels and unexposed areas in the geological model; the geotechnical designer reassesses wedge support when new joints are exposed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：地質模型應保留節理可信度及未曝光區；開挖暴露新節理後，由地工設計者重核楔塊支護需求。重量計算不包含節理剪力、地下水與支護反力，亦不等於所需錨力；先證明可動方向，再建立相應自由體圖。","observationEn":"Site practice: Retain joint-confidence levels and unexposed areas in the geological model; the geotechnical designer reassesses wedge support when new joints are exposed. Weight alone excludes joint shear, water and support reactions and is not the required anchor force; establish admissible movement before drawing the corresponding free body.","failure":"注意干擾：節理延續性低估會漏掉大楔塊，局部落石常是幾何失穩的先兆，不能以平均岩體評分忽略。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Underestimated persistence can miss a large wedge; local falls may precede geometric instability and must not be dismissed using an average rock-mass rating. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用掌子面與穹頂測繪建立三維節理面，對可能出露的塊體核對延續性與體積，不把所有交線當真實裂面。地質模型應保留節理可信度及未曝光區；開挖暴露新節理後，由地工設計者重核楔塊支護需求。","textEn":"Build three-dimensional joint planes from face and crown mapping, verifying persistence and volume of potentially daylighting blocks rather than treating every intersection as a real release surface. Retain joint-confidence levels and unexposed areas in the geological model; the geotechnical designer reassesses wedge support when new joints are exposed.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"地質模型應保留節理可信度及未曝光區；開挖暴露新節理後，由地工設計者重核楔塊支護需求。重量計算不包含節理剪力、地下水與支護反力，亦不等於所需錨力；先證明可動方向，再建立相應自由體圖。","textEn":"Retain joint-confidence levels and unexposed areas in the geological model; the geotechnical designer reassesses wedge support when new joints are exposed. Weight alone excludes joint shear, water and support reactions and is not the required anchor force; establish admissible movement before drawing the corresponding free body.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「節理楔塊的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint wedge mechanism and verification\"?","options":["用掌子面與穹頂測繪建立三維節理面，對可能出露的塊體核對延續性與體積，不把所有交線當真實裂面。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","模型配合一個監測點就證明所有地層參數正確。"],"optionsEn":["Build three-dimensional joint planes from face and crown mapping, verifying persistence and volume of potentially daylighting blocks rather than treating every intersection as a real release surface.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Matching one monitoring point proves every ground parameter is correct."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用掌子面與穹頂測繪建立三維節理面，對可能出露的塊體核對延續性與體積，不把所有交線當真實裂面。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build three-dimensional joint planes from face and crown mapping, verifying persistence and volume of potentially daylighting blocks rather than treating every intersection as a real release surface. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b178-v14-04","title":"節理楔塊的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint wedge mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「節理楔塊」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Joint wedge” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"節理延續性低估會漏掉大楔塊，局部落石常是幾何失穩的先兆，不能以平均岩體評分忽略。重量計算不包含節理剪力、地下水與支護反力，亦不等於所需錨力；先證明可動方向，再建立相應自由體圖。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Underestimated persistence can miss a large wedge; local falls may precede geometric instability and must not be dismissed using an average rock-mass rating. Weight alone excludes joint shear, water and support reactions and is not the required anchor force; establish admissible movement before drawing the corresponding free body. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：重量計算不包含節理剪力、地下水與支護反力，亦不等於所需錨力；先證明可動方向，再建立相應自由體圖。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Weight alone excludes joint shear, water and support reactions and is not the required anchor force; establish admissible movement before drawing the corresponding free body.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「完整岩石抗壓強度很高就不會有穹頂落塊。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"High intact-rock compressive strength prevents cavern-crown block falls.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"節理延續性低估會漏掉大楔塊，局部落石常是幾何失穩的先兆，不能以平均岩體評分忽略。重量計算不包含節理剪力、地下水與支護反力，亦不等於所需錨力；先證明可動方向，再建立相應自由體圖。","textEn":"Underestimated persistence can miss a large wedge; local falls may precede geometric instability and must not be dismissed using an average rock-mass rating. Weight alone excludes joint shear, water and support reactions and is not the required anchor force; establish admissible movement before drawing the corresponding free body.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「節理楔塊的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint wedge mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","節理延續性低估會漏掉大楔塊，局部落石常是幾何失穩的先兆，不能以平均岩體評分忽略。","上覆岩重全部直接落在噴凝土薄殼上。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Underestimated persistence can miss a large wedge; local falls may precede geometric instability and must not be dismissed using an average rock-mass rating.","All overburden weight acts directly on the thin shotcrete shell."],"answer":1,"explanation":"節理延續性低估會漏掉大楔塊，局部落石常是幾何失穩的先兆，不能以平均岩體評分忽略。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Underestimated persistence can miss a large wedge; local falls may precede geometric instability and must not be dismissed using an average rock-mass rating. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b178-v14-05","title":"岩拱應力的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rock-arch stress mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「岩拱應力」如何影響地下岩洞穹頂支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rock-arch stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Underground cavern crown support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"地下開挖把原先穿越洞室的應力重新分配到穹頂與側牆，岩體可形成拱狀傳力，但拱腳必須有足夠拘束。上覆地層重量提供初始應力量級，實際水平應力及構造作用則可能主導局部壓碎、剝落或高側牆變形。覆岩公式不是岩拱解析解，無法單獨預測洞周集中應力；地形、節理各向異性及施工卸載都須另行納入。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「岩拱應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Excavation redirects stresses that previously crossed the cavern into the crown and sidewalls, allowing arch-like transfer only if the abutments retain confinement. Overburden weight gives an initial stress scale, while horizontal and tectonic stresses may govern local crushing, spalling or tall-wall deformation. The overburden expression is not an arch solution and cannot predict boundary stress concentrations alone; topography, joint anisotropy and staged unloading require separate treatment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rock-arch stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設均質覆岩γ=26 kN/m³、深度H=100 m，垂直應力σv=γH=2600 kPa=2.6 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For homogeneous overburden γ=26 kN/m³ and depth H=100 m, vertical stress σv=γH=2600 kPa=2.6 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「上覆岩重全部直接落在噴凝土薄殼上。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"All overburden weight acts directly on the thin shotcrete shell.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「岩拱應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rock-arch stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-05-k1","title":"岩拱應力的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Rock-arch stress mechanism and verification","text":"地下開挖把原先穿越洞室的應力重新分配到穹頂與側牆，岩體可形成拱狀傳力，但拱腳必須有足夠拘束。上覆地層重量提供初始應力量級，實際水平應力及構造作用則可能主導局部壓碎、剝落或高側牆變形。","textEn":"Excavation redirects stresses that previously crossed the cavern into the crown and sidewalls, allowing arch-like transfer only if the abutments retain confinement. Overburden weight gives an initial stress scale, while horizontal and tectonic stresses may govern local crushing, spalling or tall-wall deformation.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：上覆岩重全部直接落在噴凝土薄殼上。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: All overburden weight acts directly on the thin shotcrete shell. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「岩拱應力的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rock-arch stress mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["上覆岩重全部直接落在噴凝土薄殼上。","洞室跨度變大時，只按跨度比例增加支護即可。","地下開挖把原先穿越洞室的應力重新分配到穹頂與側牆，岩體可形成拱狀傳力，但拱腳必須有足夠拘束。"],"optionsEn":["All overburden weight acts directly on the thin shotcrete shell.","Support only needs to increase linearly with cavern span.","Excavation redirects stresses that previously crossed the cavern into the crown and sidewalls, allowing arch-like transfer only if the abutments retain confinement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"地下開挖把原先穿越洞室的應力重新分配到穹頂與側牆，岩體可形成拱狀傳力，但拱腳必須有足夠拘束。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Excavation redirects stresses that previously crossed the cavern into the crown and sidewalls, allowing arch-like transfer only if the abutments retain confinement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b178-v14-06","title":"岩拱應力的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Rock-arch stress mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「岩拱應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rock-arch stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設均質覆岩γ=26 kN/m³、深度H=100 m，垂直應力σv=γH=2600 kPa=2.6 MPa。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For homogeneous overburden γ=26 kN/m³ and depth H=100 m, vertical stress σv=γH=2600 kPa=2.6 MPa. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對照覆岩地形與原位應力量測，追蹤穹頂及側牆收斂方向，檢查數值模型的拱腳反力位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare overburden topography and in-situ stress measurements, track crown and sidewall convergence directions, and inspect arch-abutment reactions in the numerical model.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設均質覆岩γ=26 kN/m³、深度H=100 m，垂直應力σv=γH=2600 kPa=2.6 MPa。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For homogeneous overburden γ=26 kN/m³ and depth H=100 m, vertical stress σv=γH=2600 kPa=2.6 MPa. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「岩拱應力的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rock-arch stress mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：假設均質覆岩γ=26 kN/m³、深度H=100 m，垂直應力σv=γH=2600 kPa=2.6 MPa。","噴凝土表面看起來連續就具有均勻厚度與韌性。","開口率相同的兩個交叉口一定具有相同穩定性。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: For homogeneous overburden γ=26 kN/m³ and depth H=100 m, vertical stress σv=γH=2600 kPa=2.6 MPa.","A continuous-looking shotcrete surface has uniform thickness and toughness.","Two intersections with the same opening ratio have the same stability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設均質覆岩γ=26 kN/m³、深度H=100 m，垂直應力σv=γH=2600 kPa=2.6 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For homogeneous overburden γ=26 kN/m³ and depth H=100 m, vertical stress σv=γH=2600 kPa=2.6 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b178-v14-07","title":"岩拱應力的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rock-arch stress mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「岩拱應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rock-arch stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對照覆岩地形與原位應力量測，追蹤穹頂及側牆收斂方向，檢查數值模型的拱腳反力位置。分層開挖方案須同時檢查穹頂及拱腳，不可只更新拱頂斷面；側牆開挖停留點由岩洞設計者確認。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare overburden topography and in-situ stress measurements, track crown and sidewall convergence directions, and inspect arch-abutment reactions in the numerical model. Stage analysis must update both crown and abutments, not only the roof section; the cavern designer confirms hold points for sidewall excavation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分層開挖方案須同時檢查穹頂及拱腳，不可只更新拱頂斷面；側牆開挖停留點由岩洞設計者確認。覆岩公式不是岩拱解析解，無法單獨預測洞周集中應力；地形、節理各向異性及施工卸載都須另行納入。","observationEn":"Site practice: Stage analysis must update both crown and abutments, not only the roof section; the cavern designer confirms hold points for sidewall excavation. The overburden expression is not an arch solution and cannot predict boundary stress concentrations alone; topography, joint anisotropy and staged unloading require separate treatment.","failure":"注意干擾：側牆卸載破壞拱腳拘束時，穹頂支護需求會增加；單看拱頂位移小可能漏掉側向失穩。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sidewall unloading can weaken arch confinement and increase crown-support demand; small crown movement alone may conceal a developing lateral instability. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對照覆岩地形與原位應力量測，追蹤穹頂及側牆收斂方向，檢查數值模型的拱腳反力位置。分層開挖方案須同時檢查穹頂及拱腳，不可只更新拱頂斷面；側牆開挖停留點由岩洞設計者確認。","textEn":"Compare overburden topography and in-situ stress measurements, track crown and sidewall convergence directions, and inspect arch-abutment reactions in the numerical model. Stage analysis must update both crown and abutments, not only the roof section; the cavern designer confirms hold points for sidewall excavation.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分層開挖方案須同時檢查穹頂及拱腳，不可只更新拱頂斷面；側牆開挖停留點由岩洞設計者確認。覆岩公式不是岩拱解析解，無法單獨預測洞周集中應力；地形、節理各向異性及施工卸載都須另行納入。","textEn":"Stage analysis must update both crown and abutments, not only the roof section; the cavern designer confirms hold points for sidewall excavation. The overburden expression is not an arch solution and cannot predict boundary stress concentrations alone; topography, joint anisotropy and staged unloading require separate treatment.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「岩拱應力的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rock-arch stress mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","對照覆岩地形與原位應力量測，追蹤穹頂及側牆收斂方向，檢查數值模型的拱腳反力位置。","地下岩洞不受地表搖動，所以支護不用耐震檢查。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Compare overburden topography and in-situ stress measurements, track crown and sidewall convergence directions, and inspect arch-abutment reactions in the numerical model.","Underground caverns do not experience surface shaking, so support needs no seismic checks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"對照覆岩地形與原位應力量測，追蹤穹頂及側牆收斂方向，檢查數值模型的拱腳反力位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare overburden topography and in-situ stress measurements, track crown and sidewall convergence directions, and inspect arch-abutment reactions in the numerical model. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b178-v14-08","title":"岩拱應力的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rock-arch stress mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「岩拱應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rock-arch stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"側牆卸載破壞拱腳拘束時，穹頂支護需求會增加；單看拱頂位移小可能漏掉側向失穩。覆岩公式不是岩拱解析解，無法單獨預測洞周集中應力；地形、節理各向異性及施工卸載都須另行納入。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sidewall unloading can weaken arch confinement and increase crown-support demand; small crown movement alone may conceal a developing lateral instability. The overburden expression is not an arch solution and cannot predict boundary stress concentrations alone; topography, joint anisotropy and staged unloading require separate treatment. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：覆岩公式不是岩拱解析解，無法單獨預測洞周集中應力；地形、節理各向異性及施工卸載都須另行納入。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The overburden expression is not an arch solution and cannot predict boundary stress concentrations alone; topography, joint anisotropy and staged unloading require separate treatment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「上覆岩重全部直接落在噴凝土薄殼上。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All overburden weight acts directly on the thin shotcrete shell.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"側牆卸載破壞拱腳拘束時，穹頂支護需求會增加；單看拱頂位移小可能漏掉側向失穩。覆岩公式不是岩拱解析解，無法單獨預測洞周集中應力；地形、節理各向異性及施工卸載都須另行納入。","textEn":"Sidewall unloading can weaken arch confinement and increase crown-support demand; small crown movement alone may conceal a developing lateral instability. The overburden expression is not an arch solution and cannot predict boundary stress concentrations alone; topography, joint anisotropy and staged unloading require separate treatment.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「岩拱應力的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rock-arch stress mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","洞室跨度變大時，只按跨度比例增加支護即可。","側牆卸載破壞拱腳拘束時，穹頂支護需求會增加；單看拱頂位移小可能漏掉側向失穩。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Support only needs to increase linearly with cavern span.","Sidewall unloading can weaken arch confinement and increase crown-support demand; small crown movement alone may conceal a developing lateral instability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"側牆卸載破壞拱腳拘束時，穹頂支護需求會增加；單看拱頂位移小可能漏掉側向失穩。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sidewall unloading can weaken arch confinement and increase crown-support demand; small crown movement alone may conceal a developing lateral instability. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b178-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「跨度效應的機理與驗證」與「錨索分力的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Span effect mechanism and verification\" and \"Cable support component mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b178-v14-09","title":"跨度效應的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Span effect mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「跨度效應」如何影響地下岩洞穹頂支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Span effect” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Underground cavern crown support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"增加岩洞跨度會增加支護跨越弱區的需求，也改變節理楔塊可形成的尺寸。均布荷載簡支梁的平方尺度可提醒跨度敏感度，但岩洞不是自由梁，實際承載由岩體、噴凝土及錨索共同提供，不能把梁式直接當岩洞設計公式。這個比值只對假設的梁系統成立，並非任何實際岩洞的承載力比例；尺寸放大還可能改變節理機制與施工方法。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「跨度效應」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Greater cavern span increases the distance support must bridge across weak ground and changes possible wedge dimensions. The squared-span scaling of a uniformly loaded simple beam illustrates sensitivity, but a cavern is not a free beam: rock, shotcrete and anchors share resistance, so the beam relation is not a cavern design equation. The ratio applies only to the assumed beam system, not the resistance of an actual cavern; scaling geometry can also change joint mechanisms and construction methods. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Span effect” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：僅作等載重簡支梁比較，L₁=18 m、L₂=24 m，M₂/M₁=(L₂/L₁)²=(24/18)²=1.78。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Only for equal-load simple-beam comparison, L₁=18 m and L₂=24 m give M₂/M₁=(L₂/L₁)²=(24/18)²=1.78.","failure":"常見誤解：「洞室跨度變大時，只按跨度比例增加支護即可。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Support only needs to increase linearly with cavern span.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「跨度效應」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Span effect”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-09-k1","title":"跨度效應的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Span effect mechanism and verification","text":"增加岩洞跨度會增加支護跨越弱區的需求，也改變節理楔塊可形成的尺寸。均布荷載簡支梁的平方尺度可提醒跨度敏感度，但岩洞不是自由梁，實際承載由岩體、噴凝土及錨索共同提供，不能把梁式直接當岩洞設計公式。","textEn":"Greater cavern span increases the distance support must bridge across weak ground and changes possible wedge dimensions. The squared-span scaling of a uniformly loaded simple beam illustrates sensitivity, but a cavern is not a free beam: rock, shotcrete and anchors share resistance, so the beam relation is not a cavern design equation.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：洞室跨度變大時，只按跨度比例增加支護即可。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Support only needs to increase linearly with cavern span. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「跨度效應的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Span effect mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["增加岩洞跨度會增加支護跨越弱區的需求，也改變節理楔塊可形成的尺寸。","洞室跨度變大時，只按跨度比例增加支護即可。","錨索總張力直接相加就是任意方向的支護力。"],"optionsEn":["Greater cavern span increases the distance support must bridge across weak ground and changes possible wedge dimensions.","Support only needs to increase linearly with cavern span.","Adding cable tensions directly gives support resistance in every direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"增加岩洞跨度會增加支護跨越弱區的需求，也改變節理楔塊可形成的尺寸。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Greater cavern span increases the distance support must bridge across weak ground and changes possible wedge dimensions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b178-v14-10","title":"跨度效應的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Span effect mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「跨度效應」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Span effect” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：僅作等載重簡支梁比較，L₁=18 m、L₂=24 m，M₂/M₁=(L₂/L₁)²=(24/18)²=1.78。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Only for equal-load simple-beam comparison, L₁=18 m and L₂=24 m give M₂/M₁=(L₂/L₁)²=(24/18)²=1.78. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較各跨度方案的地質暴露、楔塊幾何與支護位移，使用同一材料及邊界條件檢查敏感度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare geological exposure, wedge geometry and support displacement across span alternatives, keeping material and boundary assumptions consistent in the sensitivity study.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：僅作等載重簡支梁比較，L₁=18 m、L₂=24 m，M₂/M₁=(L₂/L₁)²=(24/18)²=1.78。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Only for equal-load simple-beam comparison, L₁=18 m and L₂=24 m give M₂/M₁=(L₂/L₁)²=(24/18)²=1.78. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「跨度效應的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Span effect mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["量到應變後乘上固定模數即可得到精確永久應力。","原創教學假設：僅作等載重簡支梁比較，L₁=18 m、L₂=24 m，M₂/M₁=(L₂/L₁)²=(24/18)²=1.78。","模型配合一個監測點就證明所有地層參數正確。"],"optionsEn":["Measured strain times one constant modulus gives exact permanent stress.","Original teaching assumptions: Only for equal-load simple-beam comparison, L₁=18 m and L₂=24 m give M₂/M₁=(L₂/L₁)²=(24/18)²=1.78.","Matching one monitoring point proves every ground parameter is correct."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：僅作等載重簡支梁比較，L₁=18 m、L₂=24 m，M₂/M₁=(L₂/L₁)²=(24/18)²=1.78。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Only for equal-load simple-beam comparison, L₁=18 m and L₂=24 m give M₂/M₁=(L₂/L₁)²=(24/18)²=1.78. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b178-v14-11","title":"跨度效應的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Span effect mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「跨度效應」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Span effect” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較各跨度方案的地質暴露、楔塊幾何與支護位移，使用同一材料及邊界條件檢查敏感度。方案比較應把模型形式與不變參數列清楚；結構及地工設計者共同確認何時必須改採三維岩體分析。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare geological exposure, wedge geometry and support displacement across span alternatives, keeping material and boundary assumptions consistent in the sensitivity study. State model form and fixed parameters in option comparisons; structural and geotechnical designers jointly decide when three-dimensional rock analysis becomes necessary. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：方案比較應把模型形式與不變參數列清楚；結構及地工設計者共同確認何時必須改採三維岩體分析。這個比值只對假設的梁系統成立，並非任何實際岩洞的承載力比例；尺寸放大還可能改變節理機制與施工方法。","observationEn":"Site practice: State model form and fixed parameters in option comparisons; structural and geotechnical designers jointly decide when three-dimensional rock analysis becomes necessary. The ratio applies only to the assumed beam system, not the resistance of an actual cavern; scaling geometry can also change joint mechanisms and construction methods.","failure":"注意干擾：把較小岩洞的支護間距原封不動放大使用，可能造成未支承塊體尺寸增加與局部超載。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Reusing small-cavern support spacing unchanged for a larger cavern may increase unsupported block size and local demand. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較各跨度方案的地質暴露、楔塊幾何與支護位移，使用同一材料及邊界條件檢查敏感度。方案比較應把模型形式與不變參數列清楚；結構及地工設計者共同確認何時必須改採三維岩體分析。","textEn":"Compare geological exposure, wedge geometry and support displacement across span alternatives, keeping material and boundary assumptions consistent in the sensitivity study. State model form and fixed parameters in option comparisons; structural and geotechnical designers jointly decide when three-dimensional rock analysis becomes necessary.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"方案比較應把模型形式與不變參數列清楚；結構及地工設計者共同確認何時必須改採三維岩體分析。這個比值只對假設的梁系統成立，並非任何實際岩洞的承載力比例；尺寸放大還可能改變節理機制與施工方法。","textEn":"State model form and fixed parameters in option comparisons; structural and geotechnical designers jointly decide when three-dimensional rock analysis becomes necessary. The ratio applies only to the assumed beam system, not the resistance of an actual cavern; scaling geometry can also change joint mechanisms and construction methods.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「跨度效應的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Span effect mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","排水量減少一定表示岩洞變得更乾燥且更穩定。","比較各跨度方案的地質暴露、楔塊幾何與支護位移，使用同一材料及邊界條件檢查敏感度。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Lower drain flow always means a drier and more stable cavern.","Compare geological exposure, wedge geometry and support displacement across span alternatives, keeping material and boundary assumptions consistent in the sensitivity study."],"answer":2,"explanation":"比較各跨度方案的地質暴露、楔塊幾何與支護位移，使用同一材料及邊界條件檢查敏感度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare geological exposure, wedge geometry and support displacement across span alternatives, keeping material and boundary assumptions consistent in the sensitivity study. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b178-v14-12","title":"跨度效應的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Span effect mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「跨度效應」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Span effect” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把較小岩洞的支護間距原封不動放大使用，可能造成未支承塊體尺寸增加與局部超載。這個比值只對假設的梁系統成立，並非任何實際岩洞的承載力比例；尺寸放大還可能改變節理機制與施工方法。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Reusing small-cavern support spacing unchanged for a larger cavern may increase unsupported block size and local demand. The ratio applies only to the assumed beam system, not the resistance of an actual cavern; scaling geometry can also change joint mechanisms and construction methods. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這個比值只對假設的梁系統成立，並非任何實際岩洞的承載力比例；尺寸放大還可能改變節理機制與施工方法。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The ratio applies only to the assumed beam system, not the resistance of an actual cavern; scaling geometry can also change joint mechanisms and construction methods.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「洞室跨度變大時，只按跨度比例增加支護即可。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Support only needs to increase linearly with cavern span.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把較小岩洞的支護間距原封不動放大使用，可能造成未支承塊體尺寸增加與局部超載。這個比值只對假設的梁系統成立，並非任何實際岩洞的承載力比例；尺寸放大還可能改變節理機制與施工方法。","textEn":"Reusing small-cavern support spacing unchanged for a larger cavern may increase unsupported block size and local demand. The ratio applies only to the assumed beam system, not the resistance of an actual cavern; scaling geometry can also change joint mechanisms and construction methods.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「跨度效應的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Span effect mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把較小岩洞的支護間距原封不動放大使用，可能造成未支承塊體尺寸增加與局部超載。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","錨索總張力直接相加就是任意方向的支護力。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing small-cavern support spacing unchanged for a larger cavern may increase unsupported block size and local demand.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Adding cable tensions directly gives support resistance in every direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把較小岩洞的支護間距原封不動放大使用，可能造成未支承塊體尺寸增加與局部超載。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Reusing small-cavern support spacing unchanged for a larger cavern may increase unsupported block size and local demand. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b178-v14-13","title":"錨索分力的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cable support component mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「錨索分力」如何影響地下岩洞穹頂支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cable support component” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Underground cavern crown support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"穹頂錨索須跨越可能移動的岩塊並錨入穩定岩體，才能提供有效拘束。錨力沿索軸傳遞，只有對抗位移方向的分量直接抗衡掉落；錨索角度也可能增加節理法向力而改變摩擦，但需要在自由體圖中明確計入。分力總和未檢查群體作用、鋼材容量或長期損失，也不代表每支錨索均勻受力；應另核對變形相容與試驗證據。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「錨索分力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Crown cables must cross the moving block and bond into stable rock to provide restraint. Force acts along the cable, and only its component opposing motion directly resists falling. Cable inclination may also increase joint normal force and friction, but that contribution must be represented explicitly in the free-body model. The component sum omits group effects, steel resistance and long-term losses and does not prove equal cable loading; check deformation compatibility and test evidence separately. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cable support component” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：4支錨索各T=150 kN、與抗落方向夾角θ=30°，有效分力R=4Tcosθ=520 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For four cables each carrying T=150 kN at θ=30° to the resisting direction, R=4Tcosθ=520 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「錨索總張力直接相加就是任意方向的支護力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding cable tensions directly gives support resistance in every direction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「錨索分力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cable support component”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-13-k1","title":"錨索分力的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Cable support component mechanism and verification","text":"穹頂錨索須跨越可能移動的岩塊並錨入穩定岩體，才能提供有效拘束。錨力沿索軸傳遞，只有對抗位移方向的分量直接抗衡掉落；錨索角度也可能增加節理法向力而改變摩擦，但需要在自由體圖中明確計入。","textEn":"Crown cables must cross the moving block and bond into stable rock to provide restraint. Force acts along the cable, and only its component opposing motion directly resists falling.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：錨索總張力直接相加就是任意方向的支護力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding cable tensions directly gives support resistance in every direction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「錨索分力的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cable support component mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["錨索總張力直接相加就是任意方向的支護力。","穹頂錨索須跨越可能移動的岩塊並錨入穩定岩體，才能提供有效拘束。","噴凝土表面看起來連續就具有均勻厚度與韌性。"],"optionsEn":["Adding cable tensions directly gives support resistance in every direction.","Crown cables must cross the moving block and bond into stable rock to provide restraint.","A continuous-looking shotcrete surface has uniform thickness and toughness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"穹頂錨索須跨越可能移動的岩塊並錨入穩定岩體，才能提供有效拘束。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Crown cables must cross the moving block and bond into stable rock to provide restraint. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b178-v14-14","title":"錨索分力的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Cable support component mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「錨索分力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cable support component” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：4支錨索各T=150 kN、與抗落方向夾角θ=30°，有效分力R=4Tcosθ=520 kN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For four cables each carrying T=150 kN at θ=30° to the resisting direction, R=4Tcosθ=520 kN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對鑽孔方向、錨碇段位置及張力紀錄，以載重試驗檢查錨固行為，再把實際角度帶入力平衡。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify bore direction, bond-zone position and force records, use load tests to assess anchorage, and insert actual angles into equilibrium.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：4支錨索各T=150 kN、與抗落方向夾角θ=30°，有效分力R=4Tcosθ=520 kN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For four cables each carrying T=150 kN at θ=30° to the resisting direction, R=4Tcosθ=520 kN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「錨索分力的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cable support component mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["開口率相同的兩個交叉口一定具有相同穩定性。","地下岩洞不受地表搖動，所以支護不用耐震檢查。","原創教學假設：4支錨索各T=150 kN、與抗落方向夾角θ=30°，有效分力R=4Tcosθ=520 kN。"],"optionsEn":["Two intersections with the same opening ratio have the same stability.","Underground caverns do not experience surface shaking, so support needs no seismic checks.","Original teaching assumptions: For four cables each carrying T=150 kN at θ=30° to the resisting direction, R=4Tcosθ=520 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：4支錨索各T=150 kN、與抗落方向夾角θ=30°，有效分力R=4Tcosθ=520 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For four cables each carrying T=150 kN at θ=30° to the resisting direction, R=4Tcosθ=520 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b178-v14-15","title":"錨索分力的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cable support component mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「錨索分力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cable support component” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對鑽孔方向、錨碇段位置及張力紀錄，以載重試驗檢查錨固行為，再把實際角度帶入力平衡。竣工圖要標出自由段、錨碇段與節理面的相對位置；地工設計者確認錨定區穩定後才放行支護驗收。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify bore direction, bond-zone position and force records, use load tests to assess anchorage, and insert actual angles into equilibrium. As-built drawings show free and bond lengths relative to joints; the geotechnical designer confirms stable anchorage before support acceptance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：竣工圖要標出自由段、錨碇段與節理面的相對位置；地工設計者確認錨定區穩定後才放行支護驗收。分力總和未檢查群體作用、鋼材容量或長期損失，也不代表每支錨索均勻受力；應另核對變形相容與試驗證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: As-built drawings show free and bond lengths relative to joints; the geotechnical designer confirms stable anchorage before support acceptance. The component sum omits group effects, steel resistance and long-term losses and does not prove equal cable loading; check deformation compatibility and test evidence separately.","failure":"注意干擾：錨碇段仍位於可動楔塊內時，張拉成功不代表已把力傳入穩定岩體，可能整組一同移動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A bond zone inside the moving wedge may tension successfully without transferring force into stable ground, allowing the whole assembly to move together. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對鑽孔方向、錨碇段位置及張力紀錄，以載重試驗檢查錨固行為，再把實際角度帶入力平衡。竣工圖要標出自由段、錨碇段與節理面的相對位置；地工設計者確認錨定區穩定後才放行支護驗收。","textEn":"Verify bore direction, bond-zone position and force records, use load tests to assess anchorage, and insert actual angles into equilibrium. As-built drawings show free and bond lengths relative to joints; the geotechnical designer confirms stable anchorage before support acceptance.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"竣工圖要標出自由段、錨碇段與節理面的相對位置；地工設計者確認錨定區穩定後才放行支護驗收。分力總和未檢查群體作用、鋼材容量或長期損失，也不代表每支錨索均勻受力；應另核對變形相容與試驗證據。","textEn":"As-built drawings show free and bond lengths relative to joints; the geotechnical designer confirms stable anchorage before support acceptance. The component sum omits group effects, steel resistance and long-term losses and does not prove equal cable loading; check deformation compatibility and test evidence separately.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「錨索分力的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cable support component mechanism and verification\"?","options":["核對鑽孔方向、錨碇段位置及張力紀錄，以載重試驗檢查錨固行為，再把實際角度帶入力平衡。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","完整岩石抗壓強度很高就不會有穹頂落塊。"],"optionsEn":["Verify bore direction, bond-zone position and force records, use load tests to assess anchorage, and insert actual angles into equilibrium.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","High intact-rock compressive strength prevents cavern-crown block falls."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對鑽孔方向、錨碇段位置及張力紀錄，以載重試驗檢查錨固行為，再把實際角度帶入力平衡。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify bore direction, bond-zone position and force records, use load tests to assess anchorage, and insert actual angles into equilibrium. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b178-v14-16","title":"錨索分力的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cable support component mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「錨索分力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cable support component” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"錨碇段仍位於可動楔塊內時，張拉成功不代表已把力傳入穩定岩體，可能整組一同移動。分力總和未檢查群體作用、鋼材容量或長期損失，也不代表每支錨索均勻受力；應另核對變形相容與試驗證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A bond zone inside the moving wedge may tension successfully without transferring force into stable ground, allowing the whole assembly to move together. The component sum omits group effects, steel resistance and long-term losses and does not prove equal cable loading; check deformation compatibility and test evidence separately. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：分力總和未檢查群體作用、鋼材容量或長期損失，也不代表每支錨索均勻受力；應另核對變形相容與試驗證據。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The component sum omits group effects, steel resistance and long-term losses and does not prove equal cable loading; check deformation compatibility and test evidence separately.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「錨索總張力直接相加就是任意方向的支護力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding cable tensions directly gives support resistance in every direction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"錨碇段仍位於可動楔塊內時，張拉成功不代表已把力傳入穩定岩體，可能整組一同移動。分力總和未檢查群體作用、鋼材容量或長期損失，也不代表每支錨索均勻受力；應另核對變形相容與試驗證據。","textEn":"A bond zone inside the moving wedge may tension successfully without transferring force into stable ground, allowing the whole assembly to move together. The component sum omits group effects, steel resistance and long-term losses and does not prove equal cable loading; check deformation compatibility and test evidence separately.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「錨索分力的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cable support component mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","錨碇段仍位於可動楔塊內時，張拉成功不代表已把力傳入穩定岩體，可能整組一同移動。","噴凝土表面看起來連續就具有均勻厚度與韌性。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A bond zone inside the moving wedge may tension successfully without transferring force into stable ground, allowing the whole assembly to move together.","A continuous-looking shotcrete surface has uniform thickness and toughness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"錨碇段仍位於可動楔塊內時，張拉成功不代表已把力傳入穩定岩體，可能整組一同移動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A bond zone inside the moving wedge may tension successfully without transferring force into stable ground, allowing the whole assembly to move together. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b178-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「噴凝土面板的機理與驗證」與「應變換算的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Shotcrete panel mechanism and verification\" and \"Strain conversion mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b178-v14-17","title":"噴凝土面板的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shotcrete panel mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「噴凝土面板」如何影響地下岩洞穹頂支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Shotcrete panel” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Underground cavern crown support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"噴凝土可束制小塊岩石並與錨桿形成局部面板系統，厚度、纖維殘餘強度及與岩面黏結共同影響其性能。面板平均壓力只能描述總荷載除以面積，不能說明孔邊沖切、薄弱處彎曲或早齡期承載是否足夠。均布壓力並不代表真正局部荷載形狀，面板需依支點與岩塊接觸重新分析；本式不能取代噴凝土構件驗算。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「噴凝土面板」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shotcrete restrains small blocks and forms local panels with rock bolts; thickness, fibre residual strength and rock adhesion jointly govern performance. Average panel pressure is only total load divided by area and does not establish resistance to punching near bolts, bending at thin spots or loading at early age. Uniform pressure does not establish the actual contact pattern; panels require analysis with their supports and block contacts, and this expression cannot replace member checks. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Shotcrete panel” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設局部岩塊荷重W=20 kN、分配面板面積A=4 m²，平均q=W/A=5 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For local block load W=20 kN distributed over panel area A=4 m², mean q=W/A=5 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「噴凝土表面看起來連續就具有均勻厚度與韌性。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A continuous-looking shotcrete surface has uniform thickness and toughness.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「噴凝土面板」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Shotcrete panel”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-17-k1","title":"噴凝土面板的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Shotcrete panel mechanism and verification","text":"噴凝土可束制小塊岩石並與錨桿形成局部面板系統，厚度、纖維殘餘強度及與岩面黏結共同影響其性能。面板平均壓力只能描述總荷載除以面積，不能說明孔邊沖切、薄弱處彎曲或早齡期承載是否足夠。","textEn":"Shotcrete restrains small blocks and forms local panels with rock bolts; thickness, fibre residual strength and rock adhesion jointly govern performance. Average panel pressure is only total load divided by area and does not establish resistance to punching near bolts, bending at thin spots or loading at early age.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：噴凝土表面看起來連續就具有均勻厚度與韌性。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A continuous-looking shotcrete surface has uniform thickness and toughness. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「噴凝土面板的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shotcrete panel mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["噴凝土表面看起來連續就具有均勻厚度與韌性。","量到應變後乘上固定模數即可得到精確永久應力。","噴凝土可束制小塊岩石並與錨桿形成局部面板系統，厚度、纖維殘餘強度及與岩面黏結共同影響其性能。"],"optionsEn":["A continuous-looking shotcrete surface has uniform thickness and toughness.","Measured strain times one constant modulus gives exact permanent stress.","Shotcrete restrains small blocks and forms local panels with rock bolts; thickness, fibre residual strength and rock adhesion jointly govern performance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"噴凝土可束制小塊岩石並與錨桿形成局部面板系統，厚度、纖維殘餘強度及與岩面黏結共同影響其性能。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shotcrete restrains small blocks and forms local panels with rock bolts; thickness, fibre residual strength and rock adhesion jointly govern performance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b178-v14-18","title":"噴凝土面板的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Shotcrete panel mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「噴凝土面板」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Shotcrete panel” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設局部岩塊荷重W=20 kN、分配面板面積A=4 m²，平均q=W/A=5 kPa。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For local block load W=20 kN distributed over panel area A=4 m², mean q=W/A=5 kPa. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用厚度針、取芯及面板試驗核對厚度與韌性，檢查錨頭附近薄弱區；將材料齡期與實際加載時間配對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check thickness and toughness using depth pins, cores and panel tests, inspect thin zones near bolt heads, and match material age to actual loading time.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設局部岩塊荷重W=20 kN、分配面板面積A=4 m²，平均q=W/A=5 kPa。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For local block load W=20 kN distributed over panel area A=4 m², mean q=W/A=5 kPa. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「噴凝土面板的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shotcrete panel mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：假設局部岩塊荷重W=20 kN、分配面板面積A=4 m²，平均q=W/A=5 kPa。","模型配合一個監測點就證明所有地層參數正確。","排水量減少一定表示岩洞變得更乾燥且更穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: For local block load W=20 kN distributed over panel area A=4 m², mean q=W/A=5 kPa.","Matching one monitoring point proves every ground parameter is correct.","Lower drain flow always means a drier and more stable cavern."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設局部岩塊荷重W=20 kN、分配面板面積A=4 m²，平均q=W/A=5 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For local block load W=20 kN distributed over panel area A=4 m², mean q=W/A=5 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b178-v14-19","title":"噴凝土面板的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shotcrete panel mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「噴凝土面板」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Shotcrete panel” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用厚度針、取芯及面板試驗核對厚度與韌性，檢查錨頭附近薄弱區；將材料齡期與實際加載時間配對。檢驗計畫應把厚度、黏結及殘餘強度分列；未達指定齡期與試驗要求前，由支護設計者確認後續開挖限制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check thickness and toughness using depth pins, cores and panel tests, inspect thin zones near bolt heads, and match material age to actual loading time. The inspection plan separates thickness, bond and residual-strength evidence; the support designer confirms excavation restrictions until specified age and test requirements are satisfied. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：檢驗計畫應把厚度、黏結及殘餘強度分列；未達指定齡期與試驗要求前，由支護設計者確認後續開挖限制。均布壓力並不代表真正局部荷載形狀，面板需依支點與岩塊接觸重新分析；本式不能取代噴凝土構件驗算。","observationEn":"Site practice: The inspection plan separates thickness, bond and residual-strength evidence; the support designer confirms excavation restrictions until specified age and test requirements are satisfied. Uniform pressure does not establish the actual contact pattern; panels require analysis with their supports and block contacts, and this expression cannot replace member checks.","failure":"注意干擾：表面平整但局部過薄或背後脫黏，會使面板突然剝落；只驗抗壓強度可能漏掉韌性不足。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A smooth surface can conceal thin spots or debonding that cause panel detachment; compressive strength alone may miss inadequate toughness. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用厚度針、取芯及面板試驗核對厚度與韌性，檢查錨頭附近薄弱區；將材料齡期與實際加載時間配對。檢驗計畫應把厚度、黏結及殘餘強度分列；未達指定齡期與試驗要求前，由支護設計者確認後續開挖限制。","textEn":"Check thickness and toughness using depth pins, cores and panel tests, inspect thin zones near bolt heads, and match material age to actual loading time. The inspection plan separates thickness, bond and residual-strength evidence; the support designer confirms excavation restrictions until specified age and test requirements are satisfied.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"檢驗計畫應把厚度、黏結及殘餘強度分列；未達指定齡期與試驗要求前，由支護設計者確認後續開挖限制。均布壓力並不代表真正局部荷載形狀，面板需依支點與岩塊接觸重新分析；本式不能取代噴凝土構件驗算。","textEn":"The inspection plan separates thickness, bond and residual-strength evidence; the support designer confirms excavation restrictions until specified age and test requirements are satisfied. Uniform pressure does not establish the actual contact pattern; panels require analysis with their supports and block contacts, and this expression cannot replace member checks.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「噴凝土面板的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shotcrete panel mechanism and verification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","用厚度針、取芯及面板試驗核對厚度與韌性，檢查錨頭附近薄弱區；將材料齡期與實際加載時間配對。","上覆岩重全部直接落在噴凝土薄殼上。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check thickness and toughness using depth pins, cores and panel tests, inspect thin zones near bolt heads, and match material age to actual loading time.","All overburden weight acts directly on the thin shotcrete shell."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用厚度針、取芯及面板試驗核對厚度與韌性，檢查錨頭附近薄弱區；將材料齡期與實際加載時間配對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check thickness and toughness using depth pins, cores and panel tests, inspect thin zones near bolt heads, and match material age to actual loading time. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b178-v14-20","title":"噴凝土面板的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shotcrete panel mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「噴凝土面板」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Shotcrete panel” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"表面平整但局部過薄或背後脫黏，會使面板突然剝落；只驗抗壓強度可能漏掉韌性不足。均布壓力並不代表真正局部荷載形狀，面板需依支點與岩塊接觸重新分析；本式不能取代噴凝土構件驗算。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A smooth surface can conceal thin spots or debonding that cause panel detachment; compressive strength alone may miss inadequate toughness. Uniform pressure does not establish the actual contact pattern; panels require analysis with their supports and block contacts, and this expression cannot replace member checks. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：均布壓力並不代表真正局部荷載形狀，面板需依支點與岩塊接觸重新分析；本式不能取代噴凝土構件驗算。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Uniform pressure does not establish the actual contact pattern; panels require analysis with their supports and block contacts, and this expression cannot replace member checks.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「噴凝土表面看起來連續就具有均勻厚度與韌性。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A continuous-looking shotcrete surface has uniform thickness and toughness.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"表面平整但局部過薄或背後脫黏，會使面板突然剝落；只驗抗壓強度可能漏掉韌性不足。均布壓力並不代表真正局部荷載形狀，面板需依支點與岩塊接觸重新分析；本式不能取代噴凝土構件驗算。","textEn":"A smooth surface can conceal thin spots or debonding that cause panel detachment; compressive strength alone may miss inadequate toughness. Uniform pressure does not establish the actual contact pattern; panels require analysis with their supports and block contacts, and this expression cannot replace member checks.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「噴凝土面板的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shotcrete panel mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","量到應變後乘上固定模數即可得到精確永久應力。","表面平整但局部過薄或背後脫黏，會使面板突然剝落；只驗抗壓強度可能漏掉韌性不足。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Measured strain times one constant modulus gives exact permanent stress.","A smooth surface can conceal thin spots or debonding that cause panel detachment; compressive strength alone may miss inadequate toughness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面平整但局部過薄或背後脫黏，會使面板突然剝落；只驗抗壓強度可能漏掉韌性不足。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A smooth surface can conceal thin spots or debonding that cause panel detachment; compressive strength alone may miss inadequate toughness. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b178-v14-21","title":"應變換算的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Strain conversion mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「應變換算」如何影響地下岩洞穹頂支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Strain conversion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Underground cavern crown support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"噴凝土或鋼構件的應變可反映支護開始參與承載的時間，但量測值包含溫度、收縮與儀器零點變化。用彈性模數換算應力前須先分離機械應變；早齡期模數及潛變不確定時，單一讀值無法唯一推回實際作用力。線彈性式只適用於所取機械增量與相應模數，不能跨越開裂或大幅潛變狀態；零讀值也不代表構件沒有歷史荷載。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「應變換算」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Support strain can indicate when shotcrete or steel begins carrying load, but readings include temperature, shrinkage and zero drift. Separate mechanical strain before multiplying by modulus; uncertain early-age stiffness and creep mean one reading cannot uniquely recover the actual force carried by the support. The elastic expression applies to the selected mechanical increment and corresponding modulus, not across cracking or major creep; a zero reading does not imply absence of historical load. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Strain conversion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設已扣除溫度與收縮、E=20 GPa、機械應變ε=50 με=50×10⁻⁶，Δσ=Eε=1 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: After temperature and shrinkage correction, assume E=20 GPa and mechanical ε=50 με=50×10⁻⁶; Δσ=Eε=1 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「量到應變後乘上固定模數即可得到精確永久應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Measured strain times one constant modulus gives exact permanent stress.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「應變換算」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Strain conversion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-21-k1","title":"應變換算的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Strain conversion mechanism and verification","text":"噴凝土或鋼構件的應變可反映支護開始參與承載的時間，但量測值包含溫度、收縮與儀器零點變化。用彈性模數換算應力前須先分離機械應變；早齡期模數及潛變不確定時，單一讀值無法唯一推回實際作用力。","textEn":"Support strain can indicate when shotcrete or steel begins carrying load, but readings include temperature, shrinkage and zero drift. Separate mechanical strain before multiplying by modulus; uncertain early-age stiffness and creep mean one reading cannot uniquely recover the actual force carried by the support.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：量到應變後乘上固定模數即可得到精確永久應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Measured strain times one constant modulus gives exact permanent stress. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「應變換算的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Strain conversion mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["噴凝土或鋼構件的應變可反映支護開始參與承載的時間，但量測值包含溫度、收縮與儀器零點變化。","量到應變後乘上固定模數即可得到精確永久應力。","開口率相同的兩個交叉口一定具有相同穩定性。"],"optionsEn":["Support strain can indicate when shotcrete or steel begins carrying load, but readings include temperature, shrinkage and zero drift.","Measured strain times one constant modulus gives exact permanent stress.","Two intersections with the same opening ratio have the same stability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"噴凝土或鋼構件的應變可反映支護開始參與承載的時間，但量測值包含溫度、收縮與儀器零點變化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Support strain can indicate when shotcrete or steel begins carrying load, but readings include temperature, shrinkage and zero drift. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b178-v14-22","title":"應變換算的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Strain conversion mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「應變換算」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Strain conversion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設已扣除溫度與收縮、E=20 GPa、機械應變ε=50 με=50×10⁻⁶，Δσ=Eε=1 MPa。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: After temperature and shrinkage correction, assume E=20 GPa and mechanical ε=50 με=50×10⁻⁶; Δσ=Eε=1 MPa. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：成對配置應變與溫度感測器，保存安裝、歸零及開挖時間；用材料試驗模數檢查換算範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Pair strain and temperature sensors, retain installation, zeroing and excavation times, and use tested moduli to bound stress conversion.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設已扣除溫度與收縮、E=20 GPa、機械應變ε=50 με=50×10⁻⁶，Δσ=Eε=1 MPa。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: After temperature and shrinkage correction, assume E=20 GPa and mechanical ε=50 με=50×10⁻⁶; Δσ=Eε=1 MPa. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「應變換算的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Strain conversion mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["地下岩洞不受地表搖動，所以支護不用耐震檢查。","原創教學假設：假設已扣除溫度與收縮、E=20 GPa、機械應變ε=50 με=50×10⁻⁶，Δσ=Eε=1 MPa。","完整岩石抗壓強度很高就不會有穹頂落塊。"],"optionsEn":["Underground caverns do not experience surface shaking, so support needs no seismic checks.","Original teaching assumptions: After temperature and shrinkage correction, assume E=20 GPa and mechanical ε=50 με=50×10⁻⁶; Δσ=Eε=1 MPa.","High intact-rock compressive strength prevents cavern-crown block falls."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設已扣除溫度與收縮、E=20 GPa、機械應變ε=50 με=50×10⁻⁶，Δσ=Eε=1 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: After temperature and shrinkage correction, assume E=20 GPa and mechanical ε=50 με=50×10⁻⁶; Δσ=Eε=1 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b178-v14-23","title":"應變換算的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Strain conversion mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「應變換算」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Strain conversion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"成對配置應變與溫度感測器，保存安裝、歸零及開挖時間；用材料試驗模數檢查換算範圍。原始讀值與修正值須分開保存；感測器更換或歸零由監測負責人記錄，設計者審核其對基準連續性的影響。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Pair strain and temperature sensors, retain installation, zeroing and excavation times, and use tested moduli to bound stress conversion. Preserve raw and corrected readings separately; the monitoring lead records sensor replacement or rezeroing, and the designer reviews its effect on baseline continuity. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：原始讀值與修正值須分開保存；感測器更換或歸零由監測負責人記錄，設計者審核其對基準連續性的影響。線彈性式只適用於所取機械增量與相應模數，不能跨越開裂或大幅潛變狀態；零讀值也不代表構件沒有歷史荷載。","observationEn":"Site practice: Preserve raw and corrected readings separately; the monitoring lead records sensor replacement or rezeroing, and the designer reviews its effect on baseline continuity. The elastic expression applies to the selected mechanical increment and corresponding modulus, not across cracking or major creep; a zero reading does not imply absence of historical load.","failure":"注意干擾：把冷卻收縮全部當成荷載應變，會誤判支護超載；錯誤歸零也可能抹掉施工前已存在的應變。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating cooling contraction entirely as load strain can falsely indicate overload, while incorrect zeroing can erase strain that existed before later excavation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"成對配置應變與溫度感測器，保存安裝、歸零及開挖時間；用材料試驗模數檢查換算範圍。原始讀值與修正值須分開保存；感測器更換或歸零由監測負責人記錄，設計者審核其對基準連續性的影響。","textEn":"Pair strain and temperature sensors, retain installation, zeroing and excavation times, and use tested moduli to bound stress conversion. Preserve raw and corrected readings separately; the monitoring lead records sensor replacement or rezeroing, and the designer reviews its effect on baseline continuity.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"原始讀值與修正值須分開保存；感測器更換或歸零由監測負責人記錄，設計者審核其對基準連續性的影響。線彈性式只適用於所取機械增量與相應模數，不能跨越開裂或大幅潛變狀態；零讀值也不代表構件沒有歷史荷載。","textEn":"Preserve raw and corrected readings separately; the monitoring lead records sensor replacement or rezeroing, and the designer reviews its effect on baseline continuity. The elastic expression applies to the selected mechanical increment and corresponding modulus, not across cracking or major creep; a zero reading does not imply absence of historical load.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「應變換算的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Strain conversion mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","洞室跨度變大時，只按跨度比例增加支護即可。","成對配置應變與溫度感測器，保存安裝、歸零及開挖時間；用材料試驗模數檢查換算範圍。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Support only needs to increase linearly with cavern span.","Pair strain and temperature sensors, retain installation, zeroing and excavation times, and use tested moduli to bound stress conversion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"成對配置應變與溫度感測器，保存安裝、歸零及開挖時間；用材料試驗模數檢查換算範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Pair strain and temperature sensors, retain installation, zeroing and excavation times, and use tested moduli to bound stress conversion. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b178-v14-24","title":"應變換算的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Strain conversion mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「應變換算」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Strain conversion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把冷卻收縮全部當成荷載應變，會誤判支護超載；錯誤歸零也可能抹掉施工前已存在的應變。線彈性式只適用於所取機械增量與相應模數，不能跨越開裂或大幅潛變狀態；零讀值也不代表構件沒有歷史荷載。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating cooling contraction entirely as load strain can falsely indicate overload, while incorrect zeroing can erase strain that existed before later excavation. The elastic expression applies to the selected mechanical increment and corresponding modulus, not across cracking or major creep; a zero reading does not imply absence of historical load. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：線彈性式只適用於所取機械增量與相應模數，不能跨越開裂或大幅潛變狀態；零讀值也不代表構件沒有歷史荷載。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The elastic expression applies to the selected mechanical increment and corresponding modulus, not across cracking or major creep; a zero reading does not imply absence of historical load.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「量到應變後乘上固定模數即可得到精確永久應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Measured strain times one constant modulus gives exact permanent stress.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把冷卻收縮全部當成荷載應變，會誤判支護超載；錯誤歸零也可能抹掉施工前已存在的應變。線彈性式只適用於所取機械增量與相應模數，不能跨越開裂或大幅潛變狀態；零讀值也不代表構件沒有歷史荷載。","textEn":"Treating cooling contraction entirely as load strain can falsely indicate overload, while incorrect zeroing can erase strain that existed before later excavation. The elastic expression applies to the selected mechanical increment and corresponding modulus, not across cracking or major creep; a zero reading does not imply absence of historical load.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「應變換算的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Strain conversion mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把冷卻收縮全部當成荷載應變，會誤判支護超載；錯誤歸零也可能抹掉施工前已存在的應變。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","開口率相同的兩個交叉口一定具有相同穩定性。"],"optionsEn":["Treating cooling contraction entirely as load strain can falsely indicate overload, while incorrect zeroing can erase strain that existed before later excavation.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Two intersections with the same opening ratio have the same stability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把冷卻收縮全部當成荷載應變，會誤判支護超載；錯誤歸零也可能抹掉施工前已存在的應變。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating cooling contraction entirely as load strain can falsely indicate overload, while incorrect zeroing can erase strain that existed before later excavation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b178-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「交叉口開口率的機理與驗證」與「反算剛度的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Intersection opening ratio mechanism and verification\" and \"Back-calculated stiffness mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b178-v14-25","title":"交叉口開口率的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Intersection opening ratio mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「交叉口開口率」如何影響地下岩洞穹頂支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Intersection opening ratio” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Underground cavern crown support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"支洞穿入大岩洞會切斷局部岩拱及支護連續性，使受力呈三維繞流。開口面積比例可用於列出幾何擾動程度，但開口位置比單一比例更重要；靠近拱腳或大型節理交會處的小開口，也可能導致顯著的應力轉移。開口率是無因次幾何指標，沒有直接的強度允收值；必須另查形狀、距離、支護連續性及交會角度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「交叉口開口率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A branch cavern interrupts local rock arching and support continuity, forcing three-dimensional load redistribution. Opening-area ratio is useful for describing geometric disturbance, but location can matter more than the ratio: a small opening near an abutment or major joint intersection may cause substantial stress transfer. Opening ratio is a dimensionless geometry descriptor without a direct strength acceptance limit; shape, spacing, support continuity and intersection angle require independent checks. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Intersection opening ratio” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設交叉開口Aopen=12 m²、參考牆面Aref=60 m²，幾何開口率r=Aopen/Aref=0.20。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For opening area Aopen=12 m² and reference wall area Aref=60 m², geometric opening ratio r=Aopen/Aref=0.20.","failure":"常見誤解：「開口率相同的兩個交叉口一定具有相同穩定性。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two intersections with the same opening ratio have the same stability.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「交叉口開口率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Intersection opening ratio”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-25-k1","title":"交叉口開口率的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Intersection opening ratio mechanism and verification","text":"支洞穿入大岩洞會切斷局部岩拱及支護連續性，使受力呈三維繞流。開口面積比例可用於列出幾何擾動程度，但開口位置比單一比例更重要；靠近拱腳或大型節理交會處的小開口，也可能導致顯著的應力轉移。","textEn":"A branch cavern interrupts local rock arching and support continuity, forcing three-dimensional load redistribution. Opening-area ratio is useful for describing geometric disturbance, but location can matter more than the ratio: a small opening near an abutment or major joint intersection may cause substantial stress transfer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：開口率相同的兩個交叉口一定具有相同穩定性。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two intersections with the same opening ratio have the same stability. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「交叉口開口率的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Intersection opening ratio mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["開口率相同的兩個交叉口一定具有相同穩定性。","支洞穿入大岩洞會切斷局部岩拱及支護連續性，使受力呈三維繞流。","模型配合一個監測點就證明所有地層參數正確。"],"optionsEn":["Two intersections with the same opening ratio have the same stability.","A branch cavern interrupts local rock arching and support continuity, forcing three-dimensional load redistribution.","Matching one monitoring point proves every ground parameter is correct."],"answer":1,"explanation":"支洞穿入大岩洞會切斷局部岩拱及支護連續性，使受力呈三維繞流。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A branch cavern interrupts local rock arching and support continuity, forcing three-dimensional load redistribution. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b178-v14-26","title":"交叉口開口率的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Intersection opening ratio mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「交叉口開口率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Intersection opening ratio” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設交叉開口Aopen=12 m²、參考牆面Aref=60 m²，幾何開口率r=Aopen/Aref=0.20。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For opening area Aopen=12 m² and reference wall area Aref=60 m², geometric opening ratio r=Aopen/Aref=0.20. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立三維開口及節理模型，量測角隅收斂與支護應變；將分部開挖順序與反應峰值對時比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Model openings and joints in three dimensions, measure corner convergence and support strain, and align response peaks with staged excavation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設交叉開口Aopen=12 m²、參考牆面Aref=60 m²，幾何開口率r=Aopen/Aref=0.20。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For opening area Aopen=12 m² and reference wall area Aref=60 m², geometric opening ratio r=Aopen/Aref=0.20. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「交叉口開口率的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Intersection opening ratio mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["排水量減少一定表示岩洞變得更乾燥且更穩定。","上覆岩重全部直接落在噴凝土薄殼上。","原創教學假設：假設交叉開口Aopen=12 m²、參考牆面Aref=60 m²，幾何開口率r=Aopen/Aref=0.20。"],"optionsEn":["Lower drain flow always means a drier and more stable cavern.","All overburden weight acts directly on the thin shotcrete shell.","Original teaching assumptions: For opening area Aopen=12 m² and reference wall area Aref=60 m², geometric opening ratio r=Aopen/Aref=0.20."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設交叉開口Aopen=12 m²、參考牆面Aref=60 m²，幾何開口率r=Aopen/Aref=0.20。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For opening area Aopen=12 m² and reference wall area Aref=60 m², geometric opening ratio r=Aopen/Aref=0.20. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b178-v14-27","title":"交叉口開口率的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Intersection opening ratio mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「交叉口開口率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Intersection opening ratio” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立三維開口及節理模型，量測角隅收斂與支護應變；將分部開挖順序與反應峰值對時比較。交叉口應有獨立地質與支護剖面；設計者確認三維荷載轉移及分部開挖停留點後，才可套用洞身標準細部。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Model openings and joints in three dimensions, measure corner convergence and support strain, and align response peaks with staged excavation. Provide dedicated geological and support sections at intersections; the designer verifies three-dimensional transfer and excavation hold points before standard tunnel details are adopted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交叉口應有獨立地質與支護剖面；設計者確認三維荷載轉移及分部開挖停留點後，才可套用洞身標準細部。開口率是無因次幾何指標，沒有直接的強度允收值；必須另查形狀、距離、支護連續性及交會角度。","observationEn":"Site practice: Provide dedicated geological and support sections at intersections; the designer verifies three-dimensional transfer and excavation hold points before standard tunnel details are adopted. Opening ratio is a dimensionless geometry descriptor without a direct strength acceptance limit; shape, spacing, support continuity and intersection angle require independent checks.","failure":"注意干擾：把交叉口當成二維直線洞身會漏掉角隅應力與拱腳削弱，裂縫可能集中在支洞交會處。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating an intersection as a two-dimensional uniform tunnel misses corner stresses and weakened abutments, allowing damage to concentrate at the branch junction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立三維開口及節理模型，量測角隅收斂與支護應變；將分部開挖順序與反應峰值對時比較。交叉口應有獨立地質與支護剖面；設計者確認三維荷載轉移及分部開挖停留點後，才可套用洞身標準細部。","textEn":"Model openings and joints in three dimensions, measure corner convergence and support strain, and align response peaks with staged excavation. Provide dedicated geological and support sections at intersections; the designer verifies three-dimensional transfer and excavation hold points before standard tunnel details are adopted.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交叉口應有獨立地質與支護剖面；設計者確認三維荷載轉移及分部開挖停留點後，才可套用洞身標準細部。開口率是無因次幾何指標，沒有直接的強度允收值；必須另查形狀、距離、支護連續性及交會角度。","textEn":"Provide dedicated geological and support sections at intersections; the designer verifies three-dimensional transfer and excavation hold points before standard tunnel details are adopted. Opening ratio is a dimensionless geometry descriptor without a direct strength acceptance limit; shape, spacing, support continuity and intersection angle require independent checks.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「交叉口開口率的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Intersection opening ratio mechanism and verification\"?","options":["建立三維開口及節理模型，量測角隅收斂與支護應變；將分部開挖順序與反應峰值對時比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","錨索總張力直接相加就是任意方向的支護力。"],"optionsEn":["Model openings and joints in three dimensions, measure corner convergence and support strain, and align response peaks with staged excavation.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adding cable tensions directly gives support resistance in every direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"建立三維開口及節理模型，量測角隅收斂與支護應變；將分部開挖順序與反應峰值對時比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Model openings and joints in three dimensions, measure corner convergence and support strain, and align response peaks with staged excavation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b178-v14-28","title":"交叉口開口率的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Intersection opening ratio mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「交叉口開口率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Intersection opening ratio” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把交叉口當成二維直線洞身會漏掉角隅應力與拱腳削弱，裂縫可能集中在支洞交會處。開口率是無因次幾何指標，沒有直接的強度允收值；必須另查形狀、距離、支護連續性及交會角度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating an intersection as a two-dimensional uniform tunnel misses corner stresses and weakened abutments, allowing damage to concentrate at the branch junction. Opening ratio is a dimensionless geometry descriptor without a direct strength acceptance limit; shape, spacing, support continuity and intersection angle require independent checks. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：開口率是無因次幾何指標，沒有直接的強度允收值；必須另查形狀、距離、支護連續性及交會角度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Opening ratio is a dimensionless geometry descriptor without a direct strength acceptance limit; shape, spacing, support continuity and intersection angle require independent checks.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「開口率相同的兩個交叉口一定具有相同穩定性。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two intersections with the same opening ratio have the same stability.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把交叉口當成二維直線洞身會漏掉角隅應力與拱腳削弱，裂縫可能集中在支洞交會處。開口率是無因次幾何指標，沒有直接的強度允收值；必須另查形狀、距離、支護連續性及交會角度。","textEn":"Treating an intersection as a two-dimensional uniform tunnel misses corner stresses and weakened abutments, allowing damage to concentrate at the branch junction. Opening ratio is a dimensionless geometry descriptor without a direct strength acceptance limit; shape, spacing, support continuity and intersection angle require independent checks.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「交叉口開口率的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Intersection opening ratio mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把交叉口當成二維直線洞身會漏掉角隅應力與拱腳削弱，裂縫可能集中在支洞交會處。","模型配合一個監測點就證明所有地層參數正確。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Treating an intersection as a two-dimensional uniform tunnel misses corner stresses and weakened abutments, allowing damage to concentrate at the branch junction.","Matching one monitoring point proves every ground parameter is correct."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把交叉口當成二維直線洞身會漏掉角隅應力與拱腳削弱，裂縫可能集中在支洞交會處。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating an intersection as a two-dimensional uniform tunnel misses corner stresses and weakened abutments, allowing damage to concentrate at the branch junction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b178-v14-29","title":"反算剛度的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Back-calculated stiffness mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「反算剛度」如何影響地下岩洞穹頂支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Back-calculated stiffness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Underground cavern crown support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"已知荷載與位移可反算等效剛度，用於檢查分析模型是否過軟或過硬，但不同的岩體參數、接縫滑移與支護剛度可能產生相似位移。只配合一個量測點會造成參數不可識別，必須用多位置與多階段反應限制合理解的範圍。此剛度屬特定階段與荷載路徑的等效值，不是岩石材料模數；若量測含剛體移動，須先移除其影響。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「反算剛度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Known force and displacement can provide an equivalent stiffness for checking whether an analysis is too soft or stiff. Different rock parameters, joint slip and support stiffness can produce similar displacement, however. Fitting one point creates an identifiability problem; several locations and construction stages are needed to constrain plausible solutions. This is an equivalent stiffness for one stage and load path, not a rock material modulus; rigid-body movement must be separated before interpreting the measurement. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Back-calculated stiffness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設對應荷載增量ΔF=500 kN、位移增量Δu=5 mm，等效k=ΔF/Δu=100 kN/mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For corresponding increments ΔF=500 kN and Δu=5 mm, equivalent stiffness k=ΔF/Δu=100 kN/mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「模型配合一個監測點就證明所有地層參數正確。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Matching one monitoring point proves every ground parameter is correct.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「反算剛度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Back-calculated stiffness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-29-k1","title":"反算剛度的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Back-calculated stiffness mechanism and verification","text":"已知荷載與位移可反算等效剛度，用於檢查分析模型是否過軟或過硬，但不同的岩體參數、接縫滑移與支護剛度可能產生相似位移。只配合一個量測點會造成參數不可識別，必須用多位置與多階段反應限制合理解的範圍。","textEn":"Known force and displacement can provide an equivalent stiffness for checking whether an analysis is too soft or stiff. Different rock parameters, joint slip and support stiffness can produce similar displacement, however.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模型配合一個監測點就證明所有地層參數正確。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Matching one monitoring point proves every ground parameter is correct. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「反算剛度的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Back-calculated stiffness mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["模型配合一個監測點就證明所有地層參數正確。","地下岩洞不受地表搖動，所以支護不用耐震檢查。","已知荷載與位移可反算等效剛度，用於檢查分析模型是否過軟或過硬，但不同的岩體參數、接縫滑移與支護剛度可能產生相似位移。"],"optionsEn":["Matching one monitoring point proves every ground parameter is correct.","Underground caverns do not experience surface shaking, so support needs no seismic checks.","Known force and displacement can provide an equivalent stiffness for checking whether an analysis is too soft or stiff."],"answer":2,"explanation":"已知荷載與位移可反算等效剛度，用於檢查分析模型是否過軟或過硬，但不同的岩體參數、接縫滑移與支護剛度可能產生相似位移。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Known force and displacement can provide an equivalent stiffness for checking whether an analysis is too soft or stiff. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b178-v14-30","title":"反算剛度的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Back-calculated stiffness mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「反算剛度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Back-calculated stiffness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設對應荷載增量ΔF=500 kN、位移增量Δu=5 mm，等效k=ΔF/Δu=100 kN/mm。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For corresponding increments ΔF=500 kN and Δu=5 mm, equivalent stiffness k=ΔF/Δu=100 kN/mm. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以多支伸長計、收斂點及支護力共同反算，保留未用於配適的資料作驗證，檢查參數是否仍具物理意義。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Back-analyse extensometers, convergence and support forces together, retaining unused observations for validation and checking that fitted parameters remain physically meaningful.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設對應荷載增量ΔF=500 kN、位移增量Δu=5 mm，等效k=ΔF/Δu=100 kN/mm。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For corresponding increments ΔF=500 kN and Δu=5 mm, equivalent stiffness k=ΔF/Δu=100 kN/mm. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「反算剛度的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Back-calculated stiffness mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：假設對應荷載增量ΔF=500 kN、位移增量Δu=5 mm，等效k=ΔF/Δu=100 kN/mm。","完整岩石抗壓強度很高就不會有穹頂落塊。","洞室跨度變大時，只按跨度比例增加支護即可。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: For corresponding increments ΔF=500 kN and Δu=5 mm, equivalent stiffness k=ΔF/Δu=100 kN/mm.","High intact-rock compressive strength prevents cavern-crown block falls.","Support only needs to increase linearly with cavern span."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設對應荷載增量ΔF=500 kN、位移增量Δu=5 mm，等效k=ΔF/Δu=100 kN/mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For corresponding increments ΔF=500 kN and Δu=5 mm, equivalent stiffness k=ΔF/Δu=100 kN/mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b178-v14-31","title":"反算剛度的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Back-calculated stiffness mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「反算剛度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Back-calculated stiffness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以多支伸長計、收斂點及支護力共同反算，保留未用於配適的資料作驗證，檢查參數是否仍具物理意義。反算報告應列參數相關性、測值誤差及獨立驗證結果；變更支護前，由設計者審核而非以自動最佳配適放行。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Back-analyse extensometers, convergence and support forces together, retaining unused observations for validation and checking that fitted parameters remain physically meaningful. Report parameter correlations, measurement error and independent validation; the designer reviews them before support changes rather than accepting an automatic best fit. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：反算報告應列參數相關性、測值誤差及獨立驗證結果；變更支護前，由設計者審核而非以自動最佳配適放行。此剛度屬特定階段與荷載路徑的等效值，不是岩石材料模數；若量測含剛體移動，須先移除其影響。","observationEn":"Site practice: Report parameter correlations, measurement error and independent validation; the designer reviews them before support changes rather than accepting an automatic best fit. This is an equivalent stiffness for one stage and load path, not a rock material modulus; rigid-body movement must be separated before interpreting the measurement.","failure":"注意干擾：任意調整岩體模數直到位移吻合，可能掩蓋錯誤支承邊界，導致下一開挖階段預測失準。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Adjusting rock modulus until displacement matches can conceal incorrect support boundaries and produce poor predictions for the next excavation stage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以多支伸長計、收斂點及支護力共同反算，保留未用於配適的資料作驗證，檢查參數是否仍具物理意義。反算報告應列參數相關性、測值誤差及獨立驗證結果；變更支護前，由設計者審核而非以自動最佳配適放行。","textEn":"Back-analyse extensometers, convergence and support forces together, retaining unused observations for validation and checking that fitted parameters remain physically meaningful. Report parameter correlations, measurement error and independent validation; the designer reviews them before support changes rather than accepting an automatic best fit.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"反算報告應列參數相關性、測值誤差及獨立驗證結果；變更支護前，由設計者審核而非以自動最佳配適放行。此剛度屬特定階段與荷載路徑的等效值，不是岩石材料模數；若量測含剛體移動，須先移除其影響。","textEn":"Report parameter correlations, measurement error and independent validation; the designer reviews them before support changes rather than accepting an automatic best fit. This is an equivalent stiffness for one stage and load path, not a rock material modulus; rigid-body movement must be separated before interpreting the measurement.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「反算剛度的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Back-calculated stiffness mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以多支伸長計、收斂點及支護力共同反算，保留未用於配適的資料作驗證，檢查參數是否仍具物理意義。","噴凝土表面看起來連續就具有均勻厚度與韌性。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Back-analyse extensometers, convergence and support forces together, retaining unused observations for validation and checking that fitted parameters remain physically meaningful.","A continuous-looking shotcrete surface has uniform thickness and toughness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以多支伸長計、收斂點及支護力共同反算，保留未用於配適的資料作驗證，檢查參數是否仍具物理意義。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Back-analyse extensometers, convergence and support forces together, retaining unused observations for validation and checking that fitted parameters remain physically meaningful. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b178-v14-32","title":"反算剛度的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Back-calculated stiffness mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「反算剛度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Back-calculated stiffness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"任意調整岩體模數直到位移吻合，可能掩蓋錯誤支承邊界，導致下一開挖階段預測失準。此剛度屬特定階段與荷載路徑的等效值，不是岩石材料模數；若量測含剛體移動，須先移除其影響。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Adjusting rock modulus until displacement matches can conceal incorrect support boundaries and produce poor predictions for the next excavation stage. This is an equivalent stiffness for one stage and load path, not a rock material modulus; rigid-body movement must be separated before interpreting the measurement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：此剛度屬特定階段與荷載路徑的等效值，不是岩石材料模數；若量測含剛體移動，須先移除其影響。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This is an equivalent stiffness for one stage and load path, not a rock material modulus; rigid-body movement must be separated before interpreting the measurement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模型配合一個監測點就證明所有地層參數正確。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Matching one monitoring point proves every ground parameter is correct.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"任意調整岩體模數直到位移吻合，可能掩蓋錯誤支承邊界，導致下一開挖階段預測失準。此剛度屬特定階段與荷載路徑的等效值，不是岩石材料模數；若量測含剛體移動，須先移除其影響。","textEn":"Adjusting rock modulus until displacement matches can conceal incorrect support boundaries and produce poor predictions for the next excavation stage. This is an equivalent stiffness for one stage and load path, not a rock material modulus; rigid-body movement must be separated before interpreting the measurement.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「反算剛度的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Back-calculated stiffness mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","地下岩洞不受地表搖動，所以支護不用耐震檢查。","任意調整岩體模數直到位移吻合，可能掩蓋錯誤支承邊界，導致下一開挖階段預測失準。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Underground caverns do not experience surface shaking, so support needs no seismic checks.","Adjusting rock modulus until displacement matches can conceal incorrect support boundaries and produce poor predictions for the next excavation stage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"任意調整岩體模數直到位移吻合，可能掩蓋錯誤支承邊界，導致下一開挖階段預測失準。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Adjusting rock modulus until displacement matches can conceal incorrect support boundaries and produce poor predictions for the next excavation stage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b178-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「地震慣性的機理與驗證」與「排水與接觸力的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Seismic inertia mechanism and verification\" and \"Drainage and contact force mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b178-v14-33","title":"地震慣性的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Seismic inertia mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「地震慣性」如何影響地下岩洞穹頂支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Seismic inertia” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Underground cavern crown support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"地震可對穹頂楔塊施加附加慣性力，也會改變節理接觸與支護受力方向。擬靜力係數提供簡化水平力，但忽略波傳、相位及結構變形差異；地下工程不能只因埋置而假設沒有地震需求，尤其需要查節理與錨固區的相對變位。擬靜力係數不是任意選用的通用常數，且此單一水平力不包含垂直作用或波傳應變；應按專案地震分析基準選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「地震慣性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Earthquakes add inertia to crown wedges and alter joint contact and support-force direction. A pseudo-static coefficient supplies a simplified horizontal force but omits wave propagation, phase and differential deformation. Burial alone does not eliminate seismic demand, particularly where joints and anchorage zones undergo relative movement. The pseudo-static coefficient is not a universal arbitrary constant, and this horizontal force excludes vertical action and wave strain; select it under the project's seismic-analysis basis. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Seismic inertia” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設楔塊重量W=312 kN、水平擬靜力係數kh=0.15，Fh=khW=46.8 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For wedge weight W=312 kN and horizontal pseudo-static coefficient kh=0.15, Fh=khW=46.8 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「地下岩洞不受地表搖動，所以支護不用耐震檢查。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Underground caverns do not experience surface shaking, so support needs no seismic checks.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「地震慣性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Seismic inertia”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-33-k1","title":"地震慣性的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Seismic inertia mechanism and verification","text":"地震可對穹頂楔塊施加附加慣性力，也會改變節理接觸與支護受力方向。擬靜力係數提供簡化水平力，但忽略波傳、相位及結構變形差異；地下工程不能只因埋置而假設沒有地震需求，尤其需要查節理與錨固區的相對變位。","textEn":"Earthquakes add inertia to crown wedges and alter joint contact and support-force direction. A pseudo-static coefficient supplies a simplified horizontal force but omits wave propagation, phase and differential deformation.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：地下岩洞不受地表搖動，所以支護不用耐震檢查。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Underground caverns do not experience surface shaking, so support needs no seismic checks. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地震慣性的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Seismic inertia mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["地震可對穹頂楔塊施加附加慣性力，也會改變節理接觸與支護受力方向。","地下岩洞不受地表搖動，所以支護不用耐震檢查。","排水量減少一定表示岩洞變得更乾燥且更穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Earthquakes add inertia to crown wedges and alter joint contact and support-force direction.","Underground caverns do not experience surface shaking, so support needs no seismic checks.","Lower drain flow always means a drier and more stable cavern."],"answer":0,"explanation":"地震可對穹頂楔塊施加附加慣性力，也會改變節理接觸與支護受力方向。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Earthquakes add inertia to crown wedges and alter joint contact and support-force direction. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b178-v14-34","title":"地震慣性的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Seismic inertia mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「地震慣性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Seismic inertia” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設楔塊重量W=312 kN、水平擬靜力係數kh=0.15，Fh=khW=46.8 kN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For wedge weight W=312 kN and horizontal pseudo-static coefficient kh=0.15, Fh=khW=46.8 kN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對場址地震需求與楔塊可動方向，分別檢查不同加速度方向的自由體圖，必要時以動力分析驗證。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check site seismic demand and admissible wedge movement, evaluate free bodies for different acceleration directions, and verify with dynamic analysis when required.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設楔塊重量W=312 kN、水平擬靜力係數kh=0.15，Fh=khW=46.8 kN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For wedge weight W=312 kN and horizontal pseudo-static coefficient kh=0.15, Fh=khW=46.8 kN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地震慣性的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Seismic inertia mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["上覆岩重全部直接落在噴凝土薄殼上。","原創教學假設：假設楔塊重量W=312 kN、水平擬靜力係數kh=0.15，Fh=khW=46.8 kN。","錨索總張力直接相加就是任意方向的支護力。"],"optionsEn":["All overburden weight acts directly on the thin shotcrete shell.","Original teaching assumptions: For wedge weight W=312 kN and horizontal pseudo-static coefficient kh=0.15, Fh=khW=46.8 kN.","Adding cable tensions directly gives support resistance in every direction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設楔塊重量W=312 kN、水平擬靜力係數kh=0.15，Fh=khW=46.8 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For wedge weight W=312 kN and horizontal pseudo-static coefficient kh=0.15, Fh=khW=46.8 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b178-v14-35","title":"地震慣性的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Seismic inertia mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「地震慣性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Seismic inertia” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對場址地震需求與楔塊可動方向，分別檢查不同加速度方向的自由體圖，必要時以動力分析驗證。交接計畫應列地震後需檢查的節理、錨頭與噴凝土區域；地工設計者確認受損機制後才核准重新開放。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check site seismic demand and admissible wedge movement, evaluate free bodies for different acceleration directions, and verify with dynamic analysis when required. Handover identifies joints, anchor heads and shotcrete zones for post-earthquake inspection; the geotechnical designer confirms damage mechanisms before reopening is approved. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接計畫應列地震後需檢查的節理、錨頭與噴凝土區域；地工設計者確認受損機制後才核准重新開放。擬靜力係數不是任意選用的通用常數，且此單一水平力不包含垂直作用或波傳應變；應按專案地震分析基準選擇。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover identifies joints, anchor heads and shotcrete zones for post-earthquake inspection; the geotechnical designer confirms damage mechanisms before reopening is approved. The pseudo-static coefficient is not a universal arbitrary constant, and this horizontal force excludes vertical action and wave strain; select it under the project's seismic-analysis basis.","failure":"注意干擾：地震使節理張開或錨索失去有效錨碇時，原有靜態安全餘裕可能消失，事件後局部落塊須重新調查。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Seismic joint opening or loss of effective anchorage can consume static margins; post-event local falls require renewed investigation of the support system. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對場址地震需求與楔塊可動方向，分別檢查不同加速度方向的自由體圖，必要時以動力分析驗證。交接計畫應列地震後需檢查的節理、錨頭與噴凝土區域；地工設計者確認受損機制後才核准重新開放。","textEn":"Check site seismic demand and admissible wedge movement, evaluate free bodies for different acceleration directions, and verify with dynamic analysis when required. Handover identifies joints, anchor heads and shotcrete zones for post-earthquake inspection; the geotechnical designer confirms damage mechanisms before reopening is approved.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接計畫應列地震後需檢查的節理、錨頭與噴凝土區域；地工設計者確認受損機制後才核准重新開放。擬靜力係數不是任意選用的通用常數，且此單一水平力不包含垂直作用或波傳應變；應按專案地震分析基準選擇。","textEn":"Handover identifies joints, anchor heads and shotcrete zones for post-earthquake inspection; the geotechnical designer confirms damage mechanisms before reopening is approved. The pseudo-static coefficient is not a universal arbitrary constant, and this horizontal force excludes vertical action and wave strain; select it under the project's seismic-analysis basis.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地震慣性的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Seismic inertia mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","量到應變後乘上固定模數即可得到精確永久應力。","核對場址地震需求與楔塊可動方向，分別檢查不同加速度方向的自由體圖，必要時以動力分析驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Measured strain times one constant modulus gives exact permanent stress.","Check site seismic demand and admissible wedge movement, evaluate free bodies for different acceleration directions, and verify with dynamic analysis when required."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對場址地震需求與楔塊可動方向，分別檢查不同加速度方向的自由體圖，必要時以動力分析驗證。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check site seismic demand and admissible wedge movement, evaluate free bodies for different acceleration directions, and verify with dynamic analysis when required. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b178-v14-36","title":"地震慣性的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Seismic inertia mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「地震慣性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Seismic inertia” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"地震使節理張開或錨索失去有效錨碇時，原有靜態安全餘裕可能消失，事件後局部落塊須重新調查。擬靜力係數不是任意選用的通用常數，且此單一水平力不包含垂直作用或波傳應變；應按專案地震分析基準選擇。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Seismic joint opening or loss of effective anchorage can consume static margins; post-event local falls require renewed investigation of the support system. The pseudo-static coefficient is not a universal arbitrary constant, and this horizontal force excludes vertical action and wave strain; select it under the project's seismic-analysis basis. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：擬靜力係數不是任意選用的通用常數，且此單一水平力不包含垂直作用或波傳應變；應按專案地震分析基準選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The pseudo-static coefficient is not a universal arbitrary constant, and this horizontal force excludes vertical action and wave strain; select it under the project's seismic-analysis basis.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「地下岩洞不受地表搖動，所以支護不用耐震檢查。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Underground caverns do not experience surface shaking, so support needs no seismic checks.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"地震使節理張開或錨索失去有效錨碇時，原有靜態安全餘裕可能消失，事件後局部落塊須重新調查。擬靜力係數不是任意選用的通用常數，且此單一水平力不包含垂直作用或波傳應變；應按專案地震分析基準選擇。","textEn":"Seismic joint opening or loss of effective anchorage can consume static margins; post-event local falls require renewed investigation of the support system. The pseudo-static coefficient is not a universal arbitrary constant, and this horizontal force excludes vertical action and wave strain; select it under the project's seismic-analysis basis.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地震慣性的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Seismic inertia mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["地震使節理張開或錨索失去有效錨碇時，原有靜態安全餘裕可能消失，事件後局部落塊須重新調查。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","排水量減少一定表示岩洞變得更乾燥且更穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Seismic joint opening or loss of effective anchorage can consume static margins; post-event local falls require renewed investigation of the support system.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Lower drain flow always means a drier and more stable cavern."],"answer":0,"explanation":"地震使節理張開或錨索失去有效錨碇時，原有靜態安全餘裕可能消失，事件後局部落塊須重新調查。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Seismic joint opening or loss of effective anchorage can consume static margins; post-event local falls require renewed investigation of the support system. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b178-v14-37","title":"排水與接觸力的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Drainage and contact force mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「排水與接觸力」如何影響地下岩洞穹頂支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Drainage and contact force” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Underground cavern crown support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"岩洞節理中的水壓會減少有效法向接觸，降低摩擦可動員程度；排水系統因此是支護性能的一部分。時間久後的沉積或結垢可使局部水壓恢復，外觀乾燥並不能證明深部節理無壓，維護應把水頭變化與支護反應一起追蹤。本式假設均勻水壓與有效接觸面積，部分張開節理需重新界定面積；若計算負值，不能把摩擦抗力當成負值繼續套用。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「排水與接觸力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Water pressure in joints reduces effective normal contact and available friction, making drainage part of support performance. Sediment or mineral buildup can restore local water pressure with time. A dry visible surface does not establish unpressurized deeper joints, so maintenance must track hydraulic head together with support response. The expression assumes uniform pressure and a defined contact area; partly open joints require revised area, and a negative result cannot be carried forward as negative friction resistance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drainage and contact force” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：法向總力N=500 kN、均勻節理水壓u=100 kPa、面積A=2 m²，N′=N−uA=300 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: With total normal force N=500 kN, uniform joint pressure u=100 kPa and area A=2 m², N′=N−uA=300 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「排水量減少一定表示岩洞變得更乾燥且更穩定。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Lower drain flow always means a drier and more stable cavern.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「排水與接觸力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drainage and contact force”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-37-k1","title":"排水與接觸力的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Drainage and contact force mechanism and verification","text":"岩洞節理中的水壓會減少有效法向接觸，降低摩擦可動員程度；排水系統因此是支護性能的一部分。時間久後的沉積或結垢可使局部水壓恢復，外觀乾燥並不能證明深部節理無壓，維護應把水頭變化與支護反應一起追蹤。","textEn":"Water pressure in joints reduces effective normal contact and available friction, making drainage part of support performance. Sediment or mineral buildup can restore local water pressure with time.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：排水量減少一定表示岩洞變得更乾燥且更穩定。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Lower drain flow always means a drier and more stable cavern. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「排水與接觸力的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Drainage and contact force mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["排水量減少一定表示岩洞變得更乾燥且更穩定。","岩洞節理中的水壓會減少有效法向接觸，降低摩擦可動員程度；排水系統因此是支護性能的一部分。","完整岩石抗壓強度很高就不會有穹頂落塊。"],"optionsEn":["Lower drain flow always means a drier and more stable cavern.","Water pressure in joints reduces effective normal contact and available friction, making drainage part of support performance.","High intact-rock compressive strength prevents cavern-crown block falls."],"answer":1,"explanation":"岩洞節理中的水壓會減少有效法向接觸，降低摩擦可動員程度；排水系統因此是支護性能的一部分。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Water pressure in joints reduces effective normal contact and available friction, making drainage part of support performance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b178-v14-38","title":"排水與接觸力的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Drainage and contact force mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「排水與接觸力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Drainage and contact force” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：法向總力N=500 kN、均勻節理水壓u=100 kPa、面積A=2 m²，N′=N−uA=300 kN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: With total normal force N=500 kN, uniform joint pressure u=100 kPa and area A=2 m², N′=N−uA=300 kN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將排水流量、水壓計與節理開合量對時比對，檢查低流量是否代表缺水或堵塞，保留清理前後資料。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare drain flow, piezometers and joint opening on one clock, distinguishing low inflow from blockage and retaining evidence before and after cleaning.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：法向總力N=500 kN、均勻節理水壓u=100 kPa、面積A=2 m²，N′=N−uA=300 kN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: With total normal force N=500 kN, uniform joint pressure u=100 kPa and area A=2 m², N′=N−uA=300 kN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「排水與接觸力的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Drainage and contact force mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["洞室跨度變大時，只按跨度比例增加支護即可。","噴凝土表面看起來連續就具有均勻厚度與韌性。","原創教學假設：法向總力N=500 kN、均勻節理水壓u=100 kPa、面積A=2 m²，N′=N−uA=300 kN。"],"optionsEn":["Support only needs to increase linearly with cavern span.","A continuous-looking shotcrete surface has uniform thickness and toughness.","Original teaching assumptions: With total normal force N=500 kN, uniform joint pressure u=100 kPa and area A=2 m², N′=N−uA=300 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：法向總力N=500 kN、均勻節理水壓u=100 kPa、面積A=2 m²，N′=N−uA=300 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: With total normal force N=500 kN, uniform joint pressure u=100 kPa and area A=2 m², N′=N−uA=300 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b178-v14-39","title":"排水與接觸力的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Drainage and contact force mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「排水與接觸力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Drainage and contact force” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將排水流量、水壓計與節理開合量對時比對，檢查低流量是否代表缺水或堵塞，保留清理前後資料。維護資料須記各排水孔的集水區與通達性；清理或封孔前，由地工及營運負責人核定對接觸力的影響。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare drain flow, piezometers and joint opening on one clock, distinguishing low inflow from blockage and retaining evidence before and after cleaning. Maintenance records identify each drain's catchment and access; geotechnical and operations leads approve the effect on contact force before cleaning or sealing drains. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：維護資料須記各排水孔的集水區與通達性；清理或封孔前，由地工及營運負責人核定對接觸力的影響。本式假設均勻水壓與有效接觸面積，部分張開節理需重新界定面積；若計算負值，不能把摩擦抗力當成負值繼續套用。","observationEn":"Site practice: Maintenance records identify each drain's catchment and access; geotechnical and operations leads approve the effect on contact force before cleaning or sealing drains. The expression assumes uniform pressure and a defined contact area; partly open joints require revised area, and a negative result cannot be carried forward as negative friction resistance.","failure":"注意干擾：排水堵塞可能使摩擦力下降而表面流量變小；若誤以為滲水改善，會錯過接觸力衰減的訊號。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Blocked drainage may reduce friction while visible flow decreases; interpreting reduced seepage as improvement can miss the loss of effective contact force. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將排水流量、水壓計與節理開合量對時比對，檢查低流量是否代表缺水或堵塞，保留清理前後資料。維護資料須記各排水孔的集水區與通達性；清理或封孔前，由地工及營運負責人核定對接觸力的影響。","textEn":"Compare drain flow, piezometers and joint opening on one clock, distinguishing low inflow from blockage and retaining evidence before and after cleaning. Maintenance records identify each drain's catchment and access; geotechnical and operations leads approve the effect on contact force before cleaning or sealing drains.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"維護資料須記各排水孔的集水區與通達性；清理或封孔前，由地工及營運負責人核定對接觸力的影響。本式假設均勻水壓與有效接觸面積，部分張開節理需重新界定面積；若計算負值，不能把摩擦抗力當成負值繼續套用。","textEn":"Maintenance records identify each drain's catchment and access; geotechnical and operations leads approve the effect on contact force before cleaning or sealing drains. The expression assumes uniform pressure and a defined contact area; partly open joints require revised area, and a negative result cannot be carried forward as negative friction resistance.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「排水與接觸力的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Drainage and contact force mechanism and verification\"?","options":["將排水流量、水壓計與節理開合量對時比對，檢查低流量是否代表缺水或堵塞，保留清理前後資料。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","開口率相同的兩個交叉口一定具有相同穩定性。"],"optionsEn":["Compare drain flow, piezometers and joint opening on one clock, distinguishing low inflow from blockage and retaining evidence before and after cleaning.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Two intersections with the same opening ratio have the same stability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將排水流量、水壓計與節理開合量對時比對，檢查低流量是否代表缺水或堵塞，保留清理前後資料。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare drain flow, piezometers and joint opening on one clock, distinguishing low inflow from blockage and retaining evidence before and after cleaning. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b178-v14-40","title":"排水與接觸力的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Drainage and contact force mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"prerequisiteIds":["b178-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「排水與接觸力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Drainage and contact force” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"排水堵塞可能使摩擦力下降而表面流量變小；若誤以為滲水改善，會錯過接觸力衰減的訊號。本式假設均勻水壓與有效接觸面積，部分張開節理需重新界定面積；若計算負值，不能把摩擦抗力當成負值繼續套用。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Blocked drainage may reduce friction while visible flow decreases; interpreting reduced seepage as improvement can miss the loss of effective contact force. The expression assumes uniform pressure and a defined contact area; partly open joints require revised area, and a negative result cannot be carried forward as negative friction resistance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本式假設均勻水壓與有效接觸面積，部分張開節理需重新界定面積；若計算負值，不能把摩擦抗力當成負值繼續套用。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The expression assumes uniform pressure and a defined contact area; partly open joints require revised area, and a negative result cannot be carried forward as negative friction resistance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「排水量減少一定表示岩洞變得更乾燥且更穩定。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Lower drain flow always means a drier and more stable cavern.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b178-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"排水堵塞可能使摩擦力下降而表面流量變小；若誤以為滲水改善，會錯過接觸力衰減的訊號。本式假設均勻水壓與有效接觸面積，部分張開節理需重新界定面積；若計算負值，不能把摩擦抗力當成負值繼續套用。","textEn":"Blocked drainage may reduce friction while visible flow decreases; interpreting reduced seepage as improvement can miss the loss of effective contact force. The expression assumes uniform pressure and a defined contact area; partly open joints require revised area, and a negative result cannot be carried forward as negative friction resistance.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]},{"id":"b178-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「排水與接觸力的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Drainage and contact force mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","排水堵塞可能使摩擦力下降而表面流量變小；若誤以為滲水改善，會錯過接觸力衰減的訊號。","完整岩石抗壓強度很高就不會有穹頂落塊。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Blocked drainage may reduce friction while visible flow decreases; interpreting reduced seepage as improvement can miss the loss of effective contact force.","High intact-rock compressive strength prevents cavern-crown block falls."],"answer":1,"explanation":"排水堵塞可能使摩擦力下降而表面流量變小；若誤以為滲水改善，會錯過接觸力衰減的訊號。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Blocked drainage may reduce friction while visible flow decreases; interpreting reduced seepage as improvement can miss the loss of effective contact force. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-geo-cavern","v14s-usace-rock","v14s-geo","v14s-landmark-b125","v14s-dsd-stanley"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
